.TH MOIRA 1 "August 2026" "moira 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moira \- Claude and Codex quota monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moira
[\fI\-\-smoke\-test\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moira
is a compact GTK4/Libadwaita application that displays Claude and Codex
quota usage, local reset times, countdowns, refresh state and weekly
exhaustion semantics.
.PP
Data is collected only from structured provider surfaces: the chained
Claude Code status\-line command and the documented Codex app\-server
read\-only rate\-limit method. Missing or invalid data is displayed as
Unavailable, Parse error or Stale \-\- never invented.
.PP
The History tab shows quota series with reset transitions and
availability states over selectable 24h/7d/30d/90d ranges and
per\-service filters, plus exact daily token statistics computed only
from official Codex account usage (Claude remains percentage\-only).
.PP
Per\-provider collection toggles and typed alert rules feed native
desktop and NTFY notification channels with deduplicated exhaustion,
recovery, reset and error events. Diagnostics are sanitized and can be
copied; history can be exported as CSV/JSON; manual update checks use
strict SemVer parsing.
.PP
The Integrations view contains the Agents section (Set up / Remove /
Test controls for Claude Code and Hermes hooks and Moira\-owned Codex
app\-server sessions, moved from the Settings view without behavior
change) and a read\-only Providers and models inventory: capability
badges per provider (activity, quota percentage, exact tokens, balance,
cost) and the Hermes main model plus discovered named providers, read
from the installed Hermes CLI (\fBhermes config get model \-\-json\fR and
\fBhermes config get providers \-\-json\fR) after a version/help probe.
Base URLs, credentials, paths and raw output are never displayed;
Claude remains percentage\-only, the Codex exact\-token badge follows
the latest typed availability observation in History (with stored exact
data or an official summary for the available state), and unknown
balance/cost is a state, never zero. DeepSeek balance
is refreshed only through the explicit Refresh balance action on
DeepSeek profile rows (Edit providers); the inventory itself makes no
\fB/user/balance\fR call, and a successful refresh never implies token,
cost or usage support.
Provider editing is available as an Edit providers view managing local
profiles (config v4) and per-profile Keyring credentials: remote base
URLs require HTTPS and reject loopback (local accepts only loopback),
blank input preserves the existing secret, removal is confirmed and
never touches Hermes files, writes are recoverable through a durable
0600 journal (persist-before-forward ordering, exact journal and
profile validation, mandatory backup cleanup, idempotent recovery at
startup through a bounded and reaped subprocess, no credential loss,
never reporting success while a journal remains), saving other
settings never wipes profiles, concurrent saves preserve each other,
and each profile row offers an explicit bounded, read-only
connection test (Keyring credential via a private child stdin pipe,
documented Models endpoints only, no inference or balance calls,
verified TLS, no redirects, no proxies, resolved-address policy,
wall-time bounds with reaping, ten sanitized states, one in-flight
plus one newest pending through an invariant-preserving coordinator
whose submits recheck shutdown before committing (close submits
nothing), whose rejections reset the row deterministically — never
stuck on "Testing…" — and whose newest-wins replacement terminates
the superseded request as cancelled through its own callback (no
silent replacement), results discarded on edit/remove/disable/
close and ephemeral — nothing persisted, single validated resolution
carried as an immutable family/socktype/proto/sockaddr target with a
direct connect and a getpeername check before any credential,
nonblocking stdin delivery inside the total deadline, strict Models
JSON and fail-closed preflight before any Keyring read or spawn).
DeepSeek profile rows add an explicit Refresh balance action against
the official read-only \fBGET https://api.deepseek.com/user/balance\fR
endpoint (Bearer auth, never the profile URL): exact Decimal-parsed
amounts rendered separately in deterministic currency order (Total,
Granted and Topped up; CNY then USD), a strict payload contract
(documented keys only, a real is_available boolean, a non-empty bounded
balance_infos array, unique CNY/USD entries, exact string amounts;
extra, missing, secret/account-bearing or malformed data is invalid),
mapping 200 to available/insufficient from is_available, 401/403 to
auth failed, 402 to insufficient without invented amounts, 429 to rate
limited, 5xx to server error, transport and TLS distinct, everything
else invalid, through the same child boundary (private stdin, single
validated resolution, peer check before TLS/headers, verified TLS, no
redirects or proxies, bounded time/body/output, reaping) with minimal
canonical JSON on stdout only; results are ephemeral (no config,
schema, History, activity, export or log write) and reuse the same
linearizable coordinator (one in-flight plus newest pending, cancelled
replacement, stale-row guards), starting from a Not checked state.
Hermes writes and financial units
are deferred. Independent Codex CLI sessions are never observed.
Inventory probes run only on page visibility and the explicit Refresh
button, off the GTK thread, bounded and newest\-wins with sanitized
translated statuses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-smoke\-test
Start the application, construct the main window, and quit after about
half a second. Intended for packaged validation; no data is written.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/moira/config.json
Versioned configuration (schema v3; normally
.IR ~/.config/moira/config.json ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/state.json
Last readings and alert deduplication keys (normally
.IR ~/.local/state/moira/state.json ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/history.sqlite3
Versioned SQLite History database (schema v4).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/activity.json
Privacy\-minimal agent activity store (schema v2).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 after a normal run or a successful
.B \-\-smoke\-test
run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moira\-claude\-statusline (1),
.BR moira\-agent\-hook (1)
